# `optim::reports::compact_summary`

Writes the one-line summary of a result; the same text as `print_summary`.

## Signature

```cpp
std::ostream &optim::reports::compact_summary(std::ostream &os, const optim::OptimaState &result);
```

## What It Does

Identical to [`optim::print_summary`](print_summary.md); it lives in `reports` so the three summary forms read together.

## Parameters

`os`
: The stream.

`result`
: The state.

## Returns

`os`.

## Practical Examples

### Example 1

A compact line.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

#include <iostream>

using namespace pluss::tils;

namespace optim = pluss::subsp::math::optim;
using Pack = optim::ParameterPack<pluss::Series>;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(4));
  const pluss::Series target = pluss::series::make({1.0, 2.0});
  const auto objective = [&](const pluss::Series &x) { return (x - target).square().sum(); };
  const auto disc = optim::constraints().nl_ineq([](const Pack &p) { return p.at("x").square().sum() - 1.0; });
  const optim::OptimaState result = optim::optima(objective, pluss::series::make({0.0, 0.0}), {}, disc);
  optim::reports::compact_summary(std::cout, result) << "\n";
}
```

### Example 2

For each of the four algorithms.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

#include <iostream>

using namespace pluss::tils;

namespace optim = pluss::subsp::math::optim;
using Pack = optim::ParameterPack<pluss::Series>;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(4));
  const pluss::Series target = pluss::series::make({1.0, 2.0});
  const auto objective = [&](const pluss::Series &x) { return (x - target).square().sum(); };
  const auto disc = optim::constraints().nl_ineq([](const Pack &p) { return p.at("x").square().sum() - 1.0; });

  for (const optim::OptimaAlgorithm a : {optim::OptimaAlgorithm::MeritMethod, optim::OptimaAlgorithm::SequentialQP, optim::OptimaAlgorithm::WorkingSet, optim::OptimaAlgorithm::InternalProtocol}) {
    optim::OptimaOptions options;
    options.algorithm = a;
    optim::reports::compact_summary(std::cout, optim::optima(objective, pluss::series::make({0.0, 0.0}), options, disc)) << "\n";
  }
}
```

### Example 3

After a failed run, the stall category is in the line.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

#include <iostream>

using namespace pluss::tils;

namespace optim = pluss::subsp::math::optim;
using Pack = optim::ParameterPack<pluss::Series>;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(4));
  const pluss::Series target = pluss::series::make({1.0, 2.0});
  const auto objective = [&](const pluss::Series &x) { return (x - target).square().sum(); };
  const auto disc = optim::constraints().nl_ineq([](const Pack &p) { return p.at("x").square().sum() - 1.0; });

  optim::OptimaOptions options;
  options.sequential_qp.max_iterations = 1;
  const optim::OptimaState result = optim::optima(objective, pluss::series::make({0.0, 0.0}), options, disc);
  optim::reports::compact_summary(std::cout, result) << "\n";
}
```

